WEBVTT

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.240
Niichan, Inui-san is making shaved ice.
Let's all have some together.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.770
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:19.700
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.340
umetsukusu jouhou
Immersing information

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.720
ikigurushii kono joukyou
This suffocating situation

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.480
jibun ga inai
I'm not here

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.610
kono sekai no bousou
The world is going out of control

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.890
tada musekinin ni toubou
Run away irresponsibly

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.500
dokoe ikuno
Where am I going?

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.900
Huriyamanu ameni
The never-ending rain

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.840
zubunure oitekareta kokoro ga
Soak the neglected heart

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.710
kuzure yuku chokuzen no koe wo kike
Listen to its voice before it collapses

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.910
sasayakana kizunade ii
I'm fine with the subtle connection

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:05.520
sotto anata wo dakishimeru kara
I will hold you gently

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:17.000
kasaneta inochi ga
yukkurito ima kokyuu shite iru
The overlapped souls breathe slowly

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.770
sobani iruyo
"I'll be by your side."

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:26.570
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:32.380
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.500
Ito from the Criminal Department
is out of the office right now.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.260
I see...

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.500
Are you sure, Ito-san?

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.970
I can't deal with his constant visits.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.040
I've got stuff to take care of.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.350
Besides...

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.460
Thanks for waiting!

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.830
There it is.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.640
What? Hey...

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.470
It's not nice of you to lie.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.440
What if I had some useful information for you?

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.440
Do you?

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.470
Nope.

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.980
Beef bowl ramen, extra sauce?

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.480
That one's...

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.890
We'll take that one.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:46.910
Got it!

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.450
Oh... Okay.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.930
I said I got it.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.320
Hey, it's gonna spill!

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.420
Ito-san, have you discovered
anything regarding my brother?

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.800
Go return that thing first.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.820
It's quiet.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.980
Most of the kids went home.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.120
I'm back!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.790
Welcome back.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.130
Hey, have a good day?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.360
Are you going to work now?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.090
Yup.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:28.460
I'm going out to dinner with Kanaru tonight.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.360
Isn't she pretty busy right now?

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.130
I heard she's representing
our school in something...

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.000
The Speech Contest.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.700
Well, she needs a break sometime.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.640
Then, I'll join you guys later with Yamasaki.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:42.910
It's near the cram school, right?

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.140
Hey.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.440
Aren't you two gonna go home?

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.450
And there it is!

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.220
Inui-san, I want strawberry, too. Don't skimp!

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:54.980
Sure.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.650
Doesn't look like you can
abandon the club yet, huh?

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:06.460
No... I'm thinking after the first show, maybe.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.500
That's in the fall, right?

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.960
Are you doing okay, academically?

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.100
You're applying to a nursing school, right?

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.110
Don't worry about me.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:19.410
My ranking shot up nearly one-hundred
spots in the last mock test.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.180
Thanks.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:21.520
Oh, really?

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.180
Where did you originally rank?

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:25.320
Let's not fret over the past.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.810
Ready to eat!

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:31.050
But honestly... I didn't do as well as last time.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.820
Doesn't that just mean everyone else did worse?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.760
I did my best!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.790
Uh-huh.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.600
Jun-kun, how's your brother doing lately?

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.570
What do you mean?

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:44.730
Megumi...

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.140
I can't ask him in person.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.410
He acts normal in front of us, but...

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.580
Not like Jun's an exception, y'know.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.340
Yeah...

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:54.480
But...

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.560
I'm sure he's worried about his lost brother.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.750
He had so many questions left to ask.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:11.990
But it looks to me like he's got
a lot more than that on his mind.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.360
Could Kanzato-kun...

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.700
He really liked Eiko-neechan.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.570
So if your brother killed her...

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.210
Sorry.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.610
I'm sorry... I shouldn't have...

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.190
It's fine. People said that for a while.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:41.620
But, we...

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.820
...still believe...

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:50.800
We have no news regarding
former chief Kanzato.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.600
I would let you know if we had.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:58.940
All I can tell you is the investigative
headquarters has dissolved.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:01.840
This used to be the office.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:06.020
The second Reverse incident,
and the missing case of the Chief...

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:11.460
We were finally able to investigate openly.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.820
It's so pathetic.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.960
I'm sorry for bothering you.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:24.770
I...

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:30.980
I'm finally feeling the ten year gap we all had.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.770
I have no idea where to look for him.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.750
No matter how hard I try to
think of places he may go to...

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.490
I can't come up with anything.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:45.980
This is actually the only...

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.060
That's how it is between brothers.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:54.890
Excuse me.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.170
Shin.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.270
I got released from the investigation team.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.140
I wanted to do at least one thing before I left.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.510
Take care of Jun, Shin.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.190
You're here. Aren't you getting out?

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:24.920
Thank you.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:41.770
Kanaru-san?

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.120
Jun-kun, hello.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.250
Do you need niichan?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:48.650
Oh, well...

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.260
It's not a big deal...

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.640
So you went to the dorms, too?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.300
Yes, but...

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.270
No one was there, huh?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.610
Megumi-san is at cram school,
Takuro-san is at work,

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.280
and Shin-niichan is...
probably at the police station.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.580
Asking about Ryo-niichan.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.820
I see.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:25.090
Why are you at home, then?

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:29.890
Ryo-niichan might come...
so I stop by every day just in case.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.800
It's probably easier to get him on the phone.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.030
But...

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.980
It's really nothing.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:51.250
Wait here.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.020
I have lots of Shin-niichan stuff to show you.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.050
Aniki...

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.880
Instead of getting it tailored to shorten it,

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:54.870
the bottom of this Red Line
Vintage model can be folded up.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.610
I'll take it.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.620
Great. Thank you.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.750
Thank you!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.000
Anyway...

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.300
Sakakiba-kun,
why do you watch me sometimes?

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.470
Well, it was unexpected.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:16.060
Huh?

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.500
I was surprised to find out you applied here,

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.610
but to top it off,
you know a lot and have good taste.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:26.170
I mean, you dress pretty conservatively.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.440
You're too flashy.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:35.250
Store clerks should be trendy, but not flashy.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.280
I see.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.360
Oh yeah, Yamasaki!

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:45.630
Are you free tonight?

00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:57.770
Did you hear Tookorin is quitting showbiz?

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:04.050
Everyone from the legendary idol
group are normal people now.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.120
I guess they were all normal to start with.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.380
That aside...

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.660
This is important.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:16.460
Do you watch the High School
Summer Baseball Tournaments?

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:17.420
No...

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:21.960
High school baseball kids
don't head slide anymore.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:26.240
Actually, some would even give up and
stop running in the middle of the field.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.270
You don't watch the national assembly, do you?

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.600
...I haven't watched anything
since half a year ago.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.480
Do you know what the Prime Minister
said after an Opposition party member

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:38.350
pointed out one of the
Minister's offensive comments?

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:42.080
"Ah, what a pain in the ass.
Who cares about that?"

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.280
No way.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.000
The heat isn't even on yet.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.590
Geez, come on now...

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.070
What a pain in the ass.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:07.010
Does this look familiar to you?

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:10.480
He looks happy.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:14.780
He was about to cry because
he just lost his balloon.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.820
Oh, really?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.820
Your brother seems like a nice person.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:23.920
Yeah.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.200
She's...

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:46.650
You've really never seen them?

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:48.150
Nope.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.080
Your brother was using them, too.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.220
I wanna know where he was getting them.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.460
What are they?

00:13:56.260 --> 00:14:00.430
So you weren't collaborating with
your brother or anything, huh?

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.870
The Reverse cases from half a year ago...

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.070
Those were you guys, weren't they?

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:07.500
You got it.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:15.420
Our leader was planning to have you help us, too.

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:16.640
No thanks.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:22.360
My brother went missing the same day.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:23.480
Apparently.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.580
Do you know where he is?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.660
Anything about him we don't know?

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.200
If we did, we'd be visiting him now.

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:03.530
Dammit! That CEO's pretending
like he isn't there again.

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:05.530
I can't see him, even if I make an appointment.

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:10.300
There's little we can do. They've been searched
once, under Sanada-san's supervision, already.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.710
I wasn't there, though.

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:13.500
Well...

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:20.940
Nikaido Eiko's research records about a mystery
drug with unknown substances and effects...

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:26.150
The pills found inside the Chief's
car, apparently the final product...

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:31.990
Suspicious or not, how did they narrow
the pill's origin to this company, anyhow?

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:36.130
Why didn't Hiiragi refuse the voluntary search?

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:43.570
We didn't report the Chief's meeting with the
people in a Hiiragi Pharmaceutical vehicle.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:47.000
I'll have to disguise myself as a deliveryman.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:09.830
That Sanada bastard is still the
leader of the investigation team.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:15.500
Could he be Kanzato Ryo's replacement sent
by headquarters to keep things under wraps?

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.270
Ito-san...

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:22.940
You aside, I could tell he wanted me kept
from the investigation this whole time.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:24.910
Even during the Hiiragi search.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:31.310
Even if I were totally incompetent,
I know more about the case

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:37.480
compared to those apathetic officer
replacements from the first Reverse incident.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:42.420
You'd have to be a complete idiot to not see that.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.830
Unless there's some reason behind it.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:48.790
Then who can be trusted?

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.000
Who knows?

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.470
The higher-ups, at least, can't be...

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:03.540
No doubt about it...
He's one of the Reverse culprits.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.910
Yes... I'm at...

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:14.830
Yo.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.500
Good evening, Sakakiba-kun.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.330
How's your training for the Skank Contest?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.240
Speech! Where's Mayu?

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:25.430
She's busy tonight.
She said hi to everyone, though.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:28.140
It's been a while since we all got together.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.470
Let's get Shin, too.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:54.490
Anything can happen now.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:09.540
We can't rely on the officials' power for this case.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:13.480
I've realized that over my past six months here.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:16.260
They're also above us, then.

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:19.710
The people involved in the
twisted Persona development.

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:24.060
I'm afraid the department we originally
belonged to at headquarters no longer exists.

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:28.760
I feel bad for Kanzato,
but it looks like time's run out.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:33.170
This must be hard for you, too, but...

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.040
It was more fun than I expected.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:37.610
So...

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.250
Where's Sotaro?

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.480
He went to see Kanzato Shin.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.530
If he needs to gather information, I could...

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:56.000
This is getting bad. Wakasa is in danger.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.320
Shiiba, any ideas?

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:01.700
Udou...

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:05.830
Jun-kun!

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.080
He'll die either way.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:42.800
Shin!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:43.770
Kanzato-kun!

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:14.090
Aniki...

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:55.510
itsukara yume miru koto
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:21:55.510 --> 00:22:00.850
Wasureta huri wo shitetan darou
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:08.160
Chiisana mado akeru yuuki mo naku
With no courage to open a small window,
I waited for a miracle.

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:12.390
Kiseki wo matteta
With no courage to open a small window,
I waited for a miracle.

00:22:13.590 --> 00:22:23.170
Ushinau mononado nakatta anohi no yona
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:23.540
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:28.570
mujakisa wa mou naikedo
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:35.120
namida wo nugutta ato niwa
After wiping away the tears

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:41.050
atarashii jibun ni deaeru
I'll be able to meet a new self

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:44.930
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
Even if I lose everything

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:51.200
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
There are still some things to discover

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:57.000
kesenai kizumo itsuka
Even the scars that remain

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:04.500
watashi rashii hokori ni dekiru
will someday become my pride

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:14.550
With eyes shut and ears covered, I seek the truth.

00:23:14.550 --> 00:23:19.190
Until we meet again, time will never end.

00:23:19.190 --> 00:23:23.460
Words thrown and sideways glances.

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:25.970
Hauling them means nothing.

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:29.440
Even if I remember, they all slip away.

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:32.210
The chosen ones stand rooted.

00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:34.510
Bound to reason.

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:37.240
Protect the gathering of illusions.
